  "question": {
    "text": "Paragraph: When potassium iodide is added to an aqueous solution of potassium ferricyanide, a reversible reaction is observed in which a complex \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) is formed. In a strong acidic medium, the equilibrium shifts completely towards \\(\\mathbf{P}\\). Addition of zinc chloride to \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) in a slightly acidic medium results in a sparingly soluble complex Q.\nQuestion: The number of zinc ions present in the molecular formula of $\\mathbf{Q}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": 2.5,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\rightarrow \\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{Zn}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]_2$\nOR\n$\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Zn}_2\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]$",
    "image": null
